# Arguments: nothing is passed by makepkg; these run at the package level.
#
# Nothing here writes to the user's home directory. On a system with several
# users, a post-install hook cannot know whose desktop to change, and doing so
# uninvited would violate the product's promise not to modify a desktop without
# being asked. The user runs `wallpaper-style install` themselves.

post_install() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'
Wallpaper Style has been installed, but it has not changed anything yet.

To set it up for your account, run:

    wallpaper-style install     # adds the background service and KWin effect
    wallpaper-style preview     # see the palette without applying it
    wallpaper-style apply       # snapshot, then apply

Or open "Wallpaper Style" from the application launcher, which does the same
with a graphical interface.

Diagnostics:  wallpaper-style doctor
Uninstall:    wallpaper-style uninstall
MESSAGE
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'
Wallpaper Style has been upgraded.

If you use the background service, run:

    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    wallpaper-style install     # idempotent; updates the service unit

Restart the control centre if it is open.
MESSAGE
}

pre_remove() {
  # Stop the watcher before its binary disappears, so systemd does not leave a
  # unit in a failing state that spams the journal. This runs as root, so it can
  # only act on system-wide state; a user session will be unaffected, and the
  # message below says how to finish the job.
  cat <<'MESSAGE'
Stopping any running Wallpaper Style service...

Before removing the package, each user who installed the service from the
package should run:

    systemctl --user disable --now wallpaper-style.service
    wallpaper-style uninstall

`uninstall` reverts the theme changes Wallpaper Style applied and removes the
KWin effect. Removing the package alone leaves the applied colours and the
effect in place, because they live in the user's own directories.
MESSAGE
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'
Wallpaper Style has been removed.

User data is untouched, since it lives outside the package:
    ~/.config/wallpaper-style     settings
    ~/.local/state/wallpaper-style snapshots and service state
    ~/.local/share/wallpaper-style installed marker
    ~/.local/share/color-schemes  generated colour schemes
    ~/.config/Kvantum             generated Kvantum themes

Delete those directories to remove the application's data completely.
MESSAGE
}
